      "message": "Hi Nicolas:\nPlease refer the following table for uart pad settings.\n\n       |       UART Module 1     |     UART Module 2       |\n-------+-------------------------+-------------------------+\nnpcx5  | UART_SL1 -\u003e 1 (DEVALTA) | UART_SL1 -\u003e 0 (DEVALTA) |\n       | UART_SL2 -\u003e 0 (DEVALTC) | UART_SL2 -\u003e 1 (DEVALTC) |\n-------+-------------------------+-------------------------+\nnpcx7  | UART_SL1 -\u003e 1 (DEVALTA) | UART_SL1 -\u003e 0 (DEVALTA) |\n       | UART_SL2 -\u003e 0 (DEVALTC) | UART_SL2 -\u003e 1 (DEVALTC) |\n       |NO_KSO09_SL-\u003e 0 (DEVALT9)|                         |\n\nI think the key is NPCX_UART_2_DEVALT_SL should be DEVALTC_UART_SL2 no matter chip is npcx5 or npcx7. In order to support wakeup through RX signals, setting NO_KSO09_SL to zero is necessary on npcx7. Move it to uart_init() might be a good way. We\u0027ll test this patch on our evb to prove it.",
